{
  "name": "ScoreAndExpUnit",
  "purpose": "Computes all 16 attention scores from Q and K vectors, finds the maximum score, and then calculates the exponential for each key based on the delta from the max.",
  "ports": [
    {
      "name": "clock",
      "direction": "input",
      "width": 1
    },
    {
      "name": "reset",
      "direction": "input",
      "width": 1
    },
    {
      "name": "valid_in",
      "direction": "input",
      "width": 1
    },
    {
      "name": "q_in",
      "direction": "input",
      "width": 8
    },
    {
      "name": "k_in",
      "direction": "input",
      "width": 128
    },
    {
      "name": "scores_out",
      "direction": "output",
      "width": 144
    },
    {
      "name": "exponentials_out",
      "direction": "output",
      "width": 256
    },
    {
      "name": "valid_out",
      "direction": "output",
      "width": 1
    }
  ],
  "dependencies": [],
  "implementation": "This module is a 7-stage pipeline. Stage 1: 16 parallel dot-product units compute the 16 scores (s9) from the input 'q_in' and 'k_in'. The two 4-bit elements of 'q_in' are broadcast to all units. Each unit performs two signed 4x4 multiplies and one 9-bit addition. The 16 scores are registered. Stages 2-5: A 4-level pipelined comparator tree finds the maximum score 'h' (s9) from the 16 registered scores. Stage 6: 16 parallel subtractors compute 'delta_i = h - s_i' (u8). The scores are passed through the pipeline to this stage. Stage 7: The 16 'delta_i' values are used to index a 256-entry, 16-bit wide ROM that stores the pre-computed EXP table from the contract. The 16 resulting exponential values (u16) and the pipelined scores are registered at the output.",
  "reference_ids": [],
  "design_prompt": "Design a pipelined Chisel RawModule 'ScoreAndExpUnit' with a fixed latency of 7 cycles. It takes 'q_in' (8-bit) and 'k_in' (128-bit) and produces 16 scores and 16 exponentials. First, compute the 16 signed 9-bit scores in parallel: s[i] = q[0]*k[i][0] + q[1]*k[i][1], where q and k elements are signed 4-bit values. Then, find the maximum score 'h' among the 16 scores using a pipelined comparator tree. Next, compute 16 delta values: delta[i] = h - s[i]. These deltas are non-negative and up to 8 bits wide, fitting within the 'exp_delta_max' bound. Use these deltas to look up 16-bit exponential values from a ROM initialized with the 'exp_table_packed_hex' from the algorithm contract. The module should output the 16 scores (packed into 144 bits) and the 16 exponentials (packed into 256 bits). Propagate a valid signal through the pipeline.",
